ed}]}^{T}.$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">$\\,{∇}_{x}f=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0+0 \\\\ 0+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2" "answer-field-5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93" :answer-field/choices ["answer-85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93" :answer/id #uuid "85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940" :answer/id #uuid "f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186208957 :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\nwith respect to $x$ at  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}.$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">$\\,{∇}_{x}f=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0 \\\\ 3+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205485 :answer-field/correct "answer-b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5" :answer/id #uuid "b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205486 :answer-field/correct "answer-785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923" :answer-field/choices ["answer-785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923" :answer/id #uuid "785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32" :question/id #uuid "41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32" :question/math-academy-id "q-269549" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=(2Ax+b)^{T}(2Ax+b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=2Ax+b.$ Then, $L(x)={y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{T}y)=2{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2Ax+b)=2A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & =(2A)^{T}\\cdot 2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & =(2A)^{T}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =4\\cdot {A}^{T}(2Ax+b) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}(2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}](2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 \\\\ -68\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06" "answer-4182ba73-9501-5f1c-9045-cd1a7928503c" "answer-679dcc5a-5a9f-55d5-aac6-b3a5f41d78af" "answer-53197217-2f27-584f-b12c-4e35c041f0cb" "answer-c6597316-83c7-5e8b-81d5-baa98c470d15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06" :answer/id #uuid "6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-24 \\\\ -68\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4182ba73-9501-5f1c-9045-cd1a7928503c" :answer/id #uuid "4182ba73-9501-5f1c-9045-cd1a7928503c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-35 & 55\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-679dcc5a-5a9f-55d5-aac6-b3a5f41d78af" :answer/id #uuid "679dcc5a-5a9f-55d5-aac6-b3a5f41d78af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53197217-2f27-584f-b12c-4e35c041f0cb" :answer/id #uuid "53197217-2f27-584f-b12c-4e35c041f0cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6597316-83c7-5e8b-81d5-baa98c470d15" :answer/id #uuid "c6597316-83c7-5e8b-81d5-baa98c470d15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}49 & -32\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d5a5695b-8296-5985-af65-b20134a9d8cb" :question/id #uuid "d5a5695b-8296-5985-af65-b20134a9d8cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-269465" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=(5Ax-b)^{T}(5Ax-b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=5Ax-b.$ Then, $L(x)={y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{T}y)=2{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5Ax-b)=5A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & =(5A)^{T}\\cdot 2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & =(5A)^{T}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =10\\cdot {A}^{T}(5Ax-b) \\\\  & =10\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}(5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}](5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 120 \\\\ 180\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6bbd1a5c-0501-5482-a310-9debd05ca9bc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6bbd1a5c-0501-5482-a310-9debd05ca9bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bbd1a5c-0501-5482-a310-9debd05ca9bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-957a9f6c-3b1e-5704-941b-815bbeb74ee2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-de485c91-3834-59a5-9cbb-f1af63ef0211" "answer-ca3252ab-ce3d-5f5e-9724-067f5f2fb76b" "answer-957a9f6c-3b1e-5704-941b-815bbeb74ee2" "answer-42dd4b42-211d-5972-b5c4-cf90c5e8012b" "answer-b2d6caca-dd94-5d02-ac30-3a83b5799cc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de485c91-3834-59a5-9cbb-f1af63ef0211" :answer/id #uuid "de485c91-3834-59a5-9cbb-f1af63ef0211" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca3252ab-ce3d-5f5e-9724-067f5f2fb76b" :answer/id #uuid "ca3252ab-ce3d-5f5e-9724-067f5f2fb76b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-957a9f6c-3b1e-5704-941b-815bbeb74ee2" :answer/id #uuid "957a9f6c-3b1e-5704-941b-815bbeb74ee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 120 \\\\ 180\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42dd4b42-211d-5972-b5c4-cf90c5e8012b" :answer/id #uuid "42dd4b42-211d-5972-b5c4-cf90c5e8012b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}120 & 0 & 180\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2d6caca-dd94-5d02-ac30-3a83b5799cc4" :answer/id #uuid "b2d6caca-dd94-5d02-ac30-3a83b5799cc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 12 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-411aabaa-bd7a-5b74-b0d5-19adca16cb89" :question/id #uuid "411aabaa-bd7a-5b74-b0d5-19adca16cb89" :question/math-academy-id "q-269470" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=(Ax-2b)^{T}(Ax-2b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=Ax-2b.$ Then, $L(x)={y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{T}y)=2{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(Ax-2b)=A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =2\\cdot {A}^{T}(Ax-2b) \\\\  & =2\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d61f281-b20f-5b2b-9b40-f631fe100b4f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d61f281-b20f-5b2b-9b40-f631fe100b4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d61f281-b20f-5b2b-9b40-f631fe100b4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-142f877f-e698-5254-93da-53589da88451" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b802d7a-2645-5ba2-9341-530841a24204" "answer-142f877f-e698-5254-93da-53589da88451" "answer-733ac048-f58d-5680-814f-d36675d8c2f1" "answer-f414dbbc-4b36-56b2-8d02-f57f2d9a1e36" "answer-9d2f0e60-7b67-503d-9ec7-438462275ae8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b802d7a-2645-5ba2-9341-530841a24204" :answer/id #uuid "3b802d7a-2645-5ba2-9341-530841a24204" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -10 & 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-142f877f-e698-5254-93da-53589da88451" :answer/id #uuid "142f877f-e698-5254-93da-53589da88451" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-733ac048-f58d-5680-814f-d36675d8c2f1" :answer/id #uuid "733ac048-f58d-5680-814f-d36675d8c2f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f414dbbc-4b36-56b2-8d02-f57f2d9a1e36" :answer/id #uuid "f414dbbc-4b36-56b2-8d02-f57f2d9a1e36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d2f0e60-7b67-503d-9ec7-438462275ae8" :answer/id #uuid "9d2f0e60-7b67-503d-9ec7-438462275ae8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c92e05a7-340f-573b-9fe1-3137e228de5f" :question/id #uuid "c92e05a7-340f-573b-9fe1-3137e228de5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-269518" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=2(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b.$ Then, $L(x)=2{y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{T}y)=4{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(Ax-b)=A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 4y \\\\  & =4\\cdot {A}^{T}(Ax-b) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 16 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-68 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2057498e-fa7c-5977-b9d8-e7c0c6099eb9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2057498e-fa7c-5977-b9d8-e7c0c6099eb9" :answer-field/id #uuid "2057498e-fa7c-5977-b9d8-e7c0c6099eb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b5373f73-c69f-5551-8e02-a40eab04c3e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-65b8247f-5cca-5ad6-b7e6-1c0348949372" "answer-b5373f73-c69f-5551-8e02-a40eab04c3e0" "answer-97adc8aa-27be-581c-8f16-71be62025db5" "answer-c5783d90-4abf-5066-b1d9-6d183ea64767" "answer-a3fd209b-0c16-51c1-a53b-64513496bb0a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65b8247f-5cca-5ad6-b7e6-1c0348949372" :answer/id #uuid "65b8247f-5cca-5ad6-b7e6-1c0348949372" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5373f73-c69f-5551-8e02-a40eab04c3e0" :answer/id #uuid "b5373f73-c69f-5551-8e02-a40eab04c3e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-68 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97adc8aa-27be-581c-8f16-71be62025db5" :answer/id #uuid "97adc8aa-27be-581c-8f16-71be62025db5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5783d90-4abf-5066-b1d9-6d183ea64767" :answer/id #uuid "c5783d90-4abf-5066-b1d9-6d183ea64767" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 49\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3fd209b-0c16-51c1-a53b-64513496bb0a" :answer/id #uuid "a3fd209b-0c16-51c1-a53b-64513496bb0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186208929 :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=2(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b.$ Then, $L(x)=2{y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{T}y)=4{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(Ax-b)=A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 4y \\\\  & =4\\cdot {A}^{T}(Ax-b) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}([\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 32 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205335 :answer-field/correct "answer-eedfdf30-92c3-5e54-aaf9-5fb07ffd1c4f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c8e551dd-aff9-5cdf-a21e-dee3bfc6a1df" "answer-952049ad-9e8a-5b7c-8a40-1b529b790b30" "answer-01c3cde9-216b-5b06-a2d7-f17bcc359a07" "answer-e0d16db9-d28a-5208-8418-ea2e4224aad3" "answer-eedfdf30-92c3-5e54-aaf9-5fb07ffd1c4f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8e551dd-aff9-5cdf-a21e-dee3bfc6a1df" :answer/id #uuid "c8e551dd-aff9-5cdf-a21e-dee3bfc6a1df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-952049ad-9e8a-5b7c-8a40-1b529b790b30" :answer/id #uuid "952049ad-9e8a-5b7c-8a40-1b529b790b30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01c3cde9-216b-5b06-a2d7-f17bcc359a07" :answer/id #uuid "01c3cde9-216b-5b06-a2d7-f17bcc359a07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0d16db9-d28a-5208-8418-ea2e4224aad3" :answer/id #uuid "e0d16db9-d28a-5208-8418-ea2e4224aad3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 32 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eedfdf30-92c3-5e54-aaf9-5fb07ffd1c4f" :answer/id #uuid "eedfdf30-92c3-5e54-aaf9-5fb07ffd1c4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 32 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186209878 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we'll extend our knowledge of gradients of scalar functions to include quadratic functions, quadratic forms, and the chain rule.\n\nConsider the (scalar) **quadratic function**\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}^T \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{x}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{A} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times n}$ is a matrix, and $\\mathbf x\\in\\mathbb R^n$ is a column vector. We wish to calculate the gradient of this function:\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf x} f = \\nabla_{\\mathbf x} \\left(\\mathbf{x}^T \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{x}\\right)\n$$\n\nWe start by showing that $f$ can be written in the expanded form \n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x}) = \\sum_{i=1}^n \\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij} x_i x_j.\n$$\n\nTo understand why this is the same as $\\mathbf x^T \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf x,$ let's first write\n![](images/39/394b4241f76616fae493bcc281cbe782c1d1a89680ef24cd2776c02302b9550d.svg)\n\nNow, we compute $\\mathbf{x}^T \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{x}$ by working step by step.\n\nFirst, we compute the product $\\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{x}$, which gives us an $n\\times 1$ column vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & ⋯ & {a}_{1n} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & ⋯ & {a}_{2n} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ {a}_{n1} & {a}_{n2} & ⋯ & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11}{x}_{1}+{a}_{12}{x}_{2}+⋯+{a}_{1n}{x}_{n} \\\\ {a}_{21}{x}_{1}+{a}_{22}{x}_{2}+⋯+{a}_{2n}{x}_{n} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {a}_{n1}{x}_{1}+{a}_{n2}{x}_{2}+⋯+{a}_{nn}{x}_{n}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{1j}{x}_{j} \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{2j}{x}_{j} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{nj}{x}_{j}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply $\\mathbf{x}^T$ by this result:\n![](images/15/15180b9898708fa3f2398a534c0e4f0a57f4466abd046b388eb7af3009e534b0.svg)\n\nEach term of this product looks like $x_i \\cdot \\displaystyle\\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij} x_j$, so the full expression becomes\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}^T \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{x} = \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i \\left( \\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij} x_j \\right) = \\sum_{i=1}^n \\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij} x_i x_j.\n$$\n\nSo, we've shown that\n\n$$\n\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{\\mathbf{x}^T \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{x} = \\sum_{i=1}^n \\sum_{j=1}^n a_{ij} x_i x_j.}\n$$\n\nLet's now discuss how this helps us to compute the gradient of $f.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186209954 :tutorial/content "We have the quadratic function\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}^T A \\mathbf{x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times n}$ is a matrix, and $\\mathbf x\\in\\mathbb R^n$ is a column vector. As we've seen, $f$ can be written in the expanded form\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x}) = \\sum_{i=1}^n \\sum_{j=1}^n A_{ij} x_i x_j.\n$$\n\nWe'll use this form to compute the gradient of $f.$\n\nTo compute the gradient $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} f$, we'll differentiate this expanded form with respect to $x_k.$ First, we express our expanded function as\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf x) =  \\sum_{i \\neq k} \\sum_{j \\neq k} A_{ij} x_i x_j \n+ \\sum_{i \\neq k} A_{ik} x_i x_k \n+ \\sum_{j \\neq k} A_{kj} x_k x_j \n+ A_{kk} x_k^2.\n$$\n\nThe idea here is to break up the double summation by isolating all the terms that involve the variable $x_k$. \n\nNotice that\n\n- the first summation is *independent* of $x_k,$\n\n- the second and third summations are *linear* in $x_k,$ and\n\n- the final term is *quadratic* in $x_k.$\n\nWe can now compute our derivative term by term in a structured way. Differentiating with respect to $x_k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{k}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{k}}[{\\sum }_{i\\ne k}{\\sum }_{j\\ne k}{A}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}+{\\sum }_{i\\ne k}{A}_{ik}{x}_{i}{x}_{k}+{\\sum }_{j\\ne k}{A}_{kj}{x}_{k}{x}_{j}+{A}_{kk}{x}_{k}^{2}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i\\ne k}{A}_{ik}{x}_{i}+{\\sum }_{j\\ne k}{A}_{kj}{x}_{j}+2{A}_{kk}{x}_{k} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i\\ne k}{A}_{ik}{x}_{i})+{A}_{kk}{x}_{k}+({\\sum }_{j\\ne k}{A}_{kj}{x}_{j})+{A}_{kk}{x}_{k} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{A}_{ik}{x}_{i}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{A}_{kj}{x}_{j} \\\\  & =({A}^{T}x)_{k}+(Ax)_{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is true for all $1\\leq k \\leq n$, we get the result\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} (\\mathbf{x}^T A \\mathbf{x}) = A^T \\mathbf{x} + A \\mathbf{x} = (A^T + A)\\mathbf x.\n$$\n\nFrom here, we have the following special cases:\n\n- If $A$ is symmetric, then $A^T = A,$ $f(\\mathbf x)$ is a quadratic form, and our result simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} (\\mathbf{x}^T A \\mathbf{x}) = 2 A \\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\n- Suppose that $A = I_n$ is the $n\\times n$ identity matrix. Then, our result for symmetric matrices simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} (\\mathbf{x}^T  \\mathbf{x}) = 2 \\mathbf{x}\n$$\n\nwhich is a result we saw in a previous lesson." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186209877 :tutorial/content "Now, let $\\mathbf{y}: \\mathbb{R}^n \\to \\mathbb{R}^q$ and $f: \\mathbb{R}^q \\to \\mathbb{R}$. Suppose we want to compute the gradient \n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} f(\\mathbf{y}(\\mathbf{x})).\n$$\n\nTo do this, we need to apply the chain rule. The chain rule for total derivatives tells us that\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\frac{\\textrm{d} f}{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{x}}}_{1 \\times n}\n= \n\\underbrace{\\frac{\\textrm{d} f}{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{y}}}_{1 \\times q}\n\\cdot \n\\underbrace{\\frac{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{y}}{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{x}}}_{q \\times n}.\n$$\n\nNow, recall that the gradient of a scalar function is the transpose of the total derivative:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} f}_{n \\times 1} = \n\\left( \\frac{\\textrm{d} f}{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{x}} \\right)^T\n$$\n\nTo derive the chain rule in terms of gradients, we apply the identity $(AB)^T = B^T A^T$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x})}^{T} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T} \\\\  & ={{{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}}_{⏟}}_{n\\times q}\\cdot {{{(\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}}_{⏟}}_{q\\times 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient chain rule is\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} f = \n\\left( \\frac{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{y}}{\\textrm{d} \\mathbf{x}} \\right)^T\n\\cdot \n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{y}} f.\n$$\n\nNote that the order matters; when expressed in the gradient form, the derivatives are applied *from right to left!*" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186208872 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186208271 :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f: \\mathbb{R}^3 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by ![](images/47/47c73d44f28380c2285b914445d6e4eed32e20e4304f8373b0e650d238497569.svg) with respect to $\\mathbf{x}$ at ![](images/06/0648ff5db79fc2b00307e99fc1b14ddbc277982db84205f281f567a9c39b1eeb.svg)"] [17592186208271 :question/worked-solution "Writing ![](images/f6/f6bba4e49e37c8115f3d5696f3763224ae83da30fa92e295da8ae2905b6cfe9a.svg), we have\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf{x})= \\mathbf{x}^TA\\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nFor a symmetric matrix $A$, the gradient of the function $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}^TA\\mathbf{x}$ with respect to $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ is\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} f(\\mathbf{x}) = 2A\\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $A$ is symmetric, we get\n![](images/b2/b21fb5c13d179b77b77ba08ccd62b4e7f47274fac9fc9ea8c39936a9e52ddcef.svg)"] [17592186208289 :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f: \\mathbb{R}^2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by\n![](images/9e/9e4b8dccd90c15d35317eb418a99dde9c43f12b8b2780e35292ecc291c10e92d.svg)\nwith respect to $\\mathbf{x}$ at  ![](images/37/37e7e5c54e3e7990b627649376f8f55a27db8a82b42b2375f99941793c92ff26.svg)"] [17592186208289 :question/worked-solution "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n![](images/71/7135a764f77153e7753bd3ab87305f8347207f12d87533565c0018588e00a00f.svg)\nwe have $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}^T A \\mathbf{x}.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} f(\\mathbf{x}) = (A^T + A)\\mathbf{x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n![](images/e5/e5e95b87bd905379b447b17e1ba8946579b85b6ab29831912c154591d5d7bde4.svg)\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at ![](images/5b/5b3d05513f25be9f2d0cc61ba21dbf3b34916f6c2fce1babc8fb4de1627171da.svg)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+0 \\\\ 0-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186208272 :question/problem "Consider the function $L: \\mathbb{R}^{3} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $L(\\mathbf{x}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b})^T(\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b})$ where \n![](images/38/38fae06690f00ec57f1c56f5b3c0f4add88d5505a991f7cbd09020364c973238.svg)\nWhat is $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} L(\\mathbf{x})$ at ![](images/62/6267a6f3c8df9f11cfa395a92d426ab1901e9048cadc6b50640fc5aafc0b59df.svg)"] [17592186208272 :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b}.$ Then, $L(\\mathbf{x}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{y}^T\\mathbf{y},$ and\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{x}} L = \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}L}{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf{x}}\\right)^T = \n\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf{y}}{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf{x}}\\right)^T \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}L}{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf{y}}\\right)^T.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf{y}}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{y}^T\\mathbf{y}\\right) = \\mathbf{y}^T \n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad \n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf{y}}{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf{x}} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf{x}} (\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\mathbf{A},\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}\\cdot y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ![](images/41/41633d52787dbf98d039bf414f07a7052fe0acf0b55c831bbaf24868b22e95df.svg), we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={A}^{T}y \\\\  & ={A}^{T}(Ax-b) \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{T}([\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 81 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186208924 :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\n with respect to $x$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$"] [17592186208924 :question/worked-solution "Writing $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]$, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}Ax.\n$$\n\nFor a symmetric matrix $A$, the gradient of the function $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax$ with respect to $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2Ax.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $A$ is symmetric, we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] [17592186208924 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-7e6596af-03f0-55a8-b320-a0ebb705a39f" :answer/id #uuid "7e6596af-03f0-55a8-b320-a0ebb705a39f"] ["answer-7e6596af-03f0-55a8-b320-a0ebb705a39f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7e6596af-03f0-55a8-b320-a0ebb705a39f" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-1a124c13-f554-5359-962c-90f7cd894e01" :answer/id #uuid "1a124c13-f554-5359-962c-90f7cd894e01"] ["answer-1a124c13-f554-5359-962c-90f7cd894e01" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1a124c13-f554-5359-962c-90f7cd894e01" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-23346f1c-daf0-53aa-8167-87d06065ca2a" :answer/id #uuid "23346f1c-daf0-53aa-8167-87d06065ca2a"] ["answer-23346f1c-daf0-53aa-8167-87d06065ca2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-23346f1c-daf0-53aa-8167-87d06065ca2a" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-e1fcfb1c-90f2-5d7d-a157-d8f5b54b8b5d" :answer/id #uuid "e1fcfb1c-90f2-5d7d-a157-d8f5b54b8b5d"] ["answer-e1fcfb1c-90f2-5d7d-a157-d8f5b54b8b5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e1fcfb1c-90f2-5d7d-a157-d8f5b54b8b5d" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"] [17592186205310 :answer-field/correct "answer-e1fcfb1c-90f2-5d7d-a157-d8f5b54b8b5d"] [17592186205310 :answer-field/choices "answer-7e6596af-03f0-55a8-b320-a0ebb705a39f"] [17592186205310 :answer-field/choices "answer-1a124c13-f554-5359-962c-90f7cd894e01"] [17592186205310 :answer-field/choices "answer-23346f1c-daf0-53aa-8167-87d06065ca2a"] [17592186205310 :answer-field/choices "answer-e1fcfb1c-90f2-5d7d-a157-d8f5b54b8b5d"] ["question-66d888b2-986e-58dd-b75b-3ffbf568a4ee" :question/id #uuid "66d888b2-986e-58dd-b75b-3ffbf568a4ee"] ["question-66d888b2-986e-58dd-b75b-3ffbf568a4ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-265764"] ["question-66d888b2-986e-58dd-b75b-3ffbf568a4ee" :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\n with respect to $x$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$"] ["question-66d888b2-986e-58dd-b75b-3ffbf568a4ee" :question/worked-solution "Writing $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}Ax.\n$$\n\nFor a symmetric matrix $A$, the gradient of the function $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax$ with respect to $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2Ax.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $A$ is symmetric, we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-66d888b2-986e-58dd-b75b-3ffbf568a4ee" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-fd1b93f4-6b48-5f90-af0f-e979b93d3583" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd1b93f4-6b48-5f90-af0f-e979b93d3583"] ["answer-7b296bdc-8919-5ab6-827d-d951a9c46e17" :answer/id #uuid "7b296bdc-8919-5ab6-827d-d951a9c46e17"] ["answer-7b296bdc-8919-5ab6-827d-d951a9c46e17" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7b296bdc-8919-5ab6-827d-d951a9c46e17" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-c4108243-e1bd-51f1-bef8-13c020e0ba37" :answer/id #uuid "c4108243-e1bd-51f1-bef8-13c020e0ba37"] ["answer-c4108243-e1bd-51f1-bef8-13c020e0ba37" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c4108243-e1bd-51f1-bef8-13c020e0ba37" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-5de37790-75ca-5675-aae7-0ff1b0d1659e" :answer/id #uuid "5de37790-75ca-5675-aae7-0ff1b0d1659e"] ["answer-5de37790-75ca-5675-aae7-0ff1b0d1659e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5de37790-75ca-5675-aae7-0ff1b0d1659e" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-87e4df02-a07b-51ac-ba3c-6c80acabaddf" :answer/id #uuid "87e4df02-a07b-51ac-ba3c-6c80acabaddf"] ["answer-87e4df02-a07b-51ac-ba3c-6c80acabaddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-87e4df02-a07b-51ac-ba3c-6c80acabaddf" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-b1503f40-d92c-57b6-99d1-6c5dcdf41eb9" :answer/id #uuid "b1503f40-d92c-57b6-99d1-6c5dcdf41eb9"] ["answer-b1503f40-d92c-57b6-99d1-6c5dcdf41eb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b1503f40-d92c-57b6-99d1-6c5dcdf41eb9" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-fd1b93f4-6b48-5f90-af0f-e979b93d3583" :answer-field