18b18-ac36-55ed-9eeb-ad23a6b9ac98" :question/math-academy-id "q-276042"] ["question-9de18b18-ac36-55ed-9eeb-ad23a6b9ac98" :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\nwith respect to $x$ at  $x={[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}.$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">$\\,{∇}_{x}f=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-9de18b18-ac36-55ed-9eeb-ad23a6b9ac98" :question/worked-solution "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0+0 \\\\ 0+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9de18b18-ac36-55ed-9eeb-ad23a6b9ac98" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2"] ["answer-85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93" :answer/id #uuid "85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93"] ["answer-85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-field-aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2" :answer-field/correct "answer-85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93"] ["answer-field-aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2" :answer-field/choices "answer-85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93"] ["answer-field-5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e"] ["answer-f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940" :answer/id #uuid "f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940"] ["answer-f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-field-5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e" :answer-field/correct "answer-f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940"] ["answer-field-5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e" :answer-field/choices "answer-f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940"] ["question-9de18b18-ac36-55ed-9eeb-ad23a6b9ac98" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2"] ["question-9de18b18-ac36-55ed-9eeb-ad23a6b9ac98" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e"] [17592186208847 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9de18b18-ac36-55ed-9eeb-ad23a6b9ac98"] [17592186208957 :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\nwith respect to $x$ at  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}.$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">$\\,{∇}_{x}f=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [17592186208957 :question/worked-solution "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0 \\\\ 3+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186208957 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5" :answer/id #uuid "b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5"] ["answer-b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5" :answer/value "2"] [17592186205485 :answer-field/correct "answer-b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5"] [17592186205485 :answer-field/choices "answer-b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5"] ["answer-785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923" :answer/id #uuid "785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923"] ["answer-785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923" :answer/value "3"] [17592186205486 :answer-field/correct "answer-785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923"] [17592186205486 :answer-field/choices "answer-785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923"] ["question-41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32" :question/id #uuid "41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32"] ["question-41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32" :question/math-academy-id "q-269549"] ["question-41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=(2Ax+b)^{T}(2Ax+b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$"] ["question-41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=2Ax+b.$ Then, $L(x)={y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{T}y)=2{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2Ax+b)=2A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & =(2A)^{T}\\cdot 2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & =(2A)^{T}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =4\\cdot {A}^{T}(2Ax+b) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}(2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}](2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 \\\\ -68\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa"] ["answer-6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06" :answer/id #uuid "6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06"] ["answer-6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-24 \\\\ -68\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-4182ba73-9501-5f1c-9045-cd1a7928503c" :answer/id #uuid "4182ba73-9501-5f1c-9045-cd1a7928503c"] ["answer-4182ba73-9501-5f1c-9045-cd1a7928503c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4182ba73-9501-5f1c-9045-cd1a7928503c" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-35 & 55\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-679dcc5a-5a9f-55d5-aac6-b3a5f41d78af" :answer/id #uuid "679dcc5a-5a9f-55d5-aac6-b3a5f41d78af"] ["answer-679dcc5a-5a9f-55d5-aac6-b3a5f41d78af" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-679dcc5a-5a9f-55d5-aac6-b3a5f41d78af" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-53197217-2f27-584f-b12c-4e35c041f0cb" :answer/id #uuid "53197217-2f27-584f-b12c-4e35c041f0cb"] ["answer-53197217-2f27-584f-b12c-4e35c041f0cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-53197217-2f27-584f-b12c-4e35c041f0cb" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-c6597316-83c7-5e8b-81d5-baa98c470d15" :answer/id #uuid "c6597316-83c7-5e8b-81d5-baa98c470d15"] ["answer-c6597316-83c7-5e8b-81d5-baa98c470d15" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c6597316-83c7-5e8b-81d5-baa98c470d15" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}49 & -32\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/correct "answer-6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06"] ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06"] ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-4182ba73-9501-5f1c-9045-cd1a7928503c"] ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-679dcc5a-5a9f-55d5-aac6-b3a5f41d78af"] ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-53197217-2f27-584f-b12c-4e35c041f0cb"] ["answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/choices "answer-c6597316-83c7-5e8b-81d5-baa98c470d15"] ["question-41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa"] [17592186208848 :knowledge-point/questions "question-41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32"] ["question-d5a5695b-8296-5985-af65-b20134a9d8cb" :question/id #uuid "d5a5695b-8296-5985-af65-b20134a9d8cb"] ["question-d5a5695b-8296-5985-af65-b20134a9d8cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-269465"] ["question-d5a5695b-8296-5985-af65-b20134a9d8cb" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=(5Ax-b)^{T}(5Ax-b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$"] ["question-d5a5695b-8296-5985-af65-b20134a9d8cb" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=5Ax-b.$ Then, $L(x)={y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{T}y)=2{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5Ax-b)=5A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & =(5A)^{T}\\cdot 2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & =(5A)^{T}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =10\\cdot {A}^{T}(5Ax-b) \\\\  & =10\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}(5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}](5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 120 \\\\ 180\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-d5a5695b-8296-5985-af65-b20134a9d8cb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-6bbd1a5c-0501-5482-a310-9debd05ca9bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bbd1a5c-0501-5482-a310-9debd05ca9bc"] ["answer-de485c91-3834-59a5-9cbb-f1af63ef0211" :answer/id #uuid "de485c91-3834-59a5-9cbb-f1af63ef0211"] ["answer-de485c91-3834-59a5-9cbb-f1af63ef0211" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-de485c91-3834-59a5-9cbb-f1af63ef0211" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-ca3252ab-ce3d-5f